# Optional. Copy to .env.local (gitignored) only if you need to override the API address.
#
# When unset, the app finds the backend (port 3000) on its own during development:
#   web browser     → the host the page was opened from (localhost on desktop)
#   phone/emulator  → the computer running `npx expo start`
#                     (with --localhost: Android emulator → 10.0.2.2,
#                      Android phone on USB → localhost via `npm run android:usb`)
#
# Set it for:
#   - deployed builds:  EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://<your-api>.onrender.com
#   - tunnels, which don't forward the backend on their own:
#       VS Code Ports panel, port 3000 set to Public → https://<id>-3000.<region>.devtunnels.ms
#   - a backend on a different computer or port
#
# Restart with `npx expo start --clear` after changing it.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://<your-api>.onrender.com
